#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186614572 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae53b6fa-2b2e-5727-b3e0-99696a2b064a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae53b6fa-2b2e-5727-b3e0-99696a2b064a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x^2+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614250} :answer-field/id #uuid "57da137f-3123-5819-8a68-9d86a5ddc7fd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51a00dc5-3c72-598a-b930-f432cd6789b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-321392" :question/problem "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cot}⁡t=x \\\\ y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡t=y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${csc}^{2}⁡t=1+{cot}^{2}⁡t$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{csc}^{2}⁡t & =1+{cot}^{2}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡t & =\\sqrt{1+{cot}^{2}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe used here that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡t>0$ and $\\operatorname{cot}⁡t>0$ in the range $0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\nNow, substituting $\\operatorname{cot}⁡t=x$ and $\\operatorname{csc}⁡t=y$ into this formula, we obtain\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{\\,1+{x}^{2}\\,}.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is \n$y=\\sqrt{\\,1+{x}^{2}\\,}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186614627 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "166b25cf-c407-543b-aa90-566de2c4f9e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+5)(x-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613939} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8349f5-d1fe-5b30-92f7-3f9d88f1bd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+9)(x-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613992} {:answer/id #uuid "4d8553b2-2dd1-5d2f-8a2c-675cedde9548" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+15)(x-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614050} {:answer/id #uuid "53497cc2-6e1f-5ac6-adc0-54bbcaea8d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=(x-5)(x-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614060} {:answer/id #uuid "c3047b0e-e7ff-5816-add3-bad0a5f5c15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+3)(x-15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f8349f5-d1fe-5b30-92f7-3f9d88f1bd90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+9)(x-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613992} :answer-field/id #uuid "e798a191-21c6-5f5e-a651-a872363a8f71" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186614529}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c7696f36-8681-5da2-87b0-f8726cfb81ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-102657" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the curve defined parametrically by\n\n$$\nx=2t-3,\\,\\,\\,y=(t-4)(t+3),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x &=2t-3\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{x+3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{x+3}{2}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(\\frac{x+3}{2}-4)(\\frac{x+3}{2}+3) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{x+3-8}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{x+3+6}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\left(\\frac{x-5}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{x+9}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(x+9)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{1}{4}(x+9)(x-5).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616134 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28cdf725-7ed0-51d6-9870-e5ccbf9504c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/db/dbe7b637ffba21e9eafebd513cb454004b1a9b72f33b20a30e242af73103cf75.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615632} {:answer/id #uuid "61b9636e-1616-5373-8a4c-164f8878bb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d42d80f53ee904ea12475ae64e9bde55845b7c9974a303535882f6f385478abd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615736} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa39e64-df93-503a-b2bd-b29ff4fa3bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/53/53cfd66db8c9ea7cf1277fb79d39038531bf6f09c37bdb98aee2f26df3d8b64d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615801} {:answer/id #uuid "c56a3112-612f-5ac6-b395-5f93b08830dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/666b01e96a9a9fc8d55e07dbdd3e48babc8cff795985d829486e03969aa13f2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615927} {:answer/id #uuid "d855639e-907f-5c6f-b6cb-38c02ef6e0b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0b5c0c9807708aa4d4c4ebffd61b0f94b6c044c0e3b3e5cd471c459d87d60b6c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61b9636e-1616-5373-8a4c-164f8878bb2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d42d80f53ee904ea12475ae64e9bde55845b7c9974a303535882f6f385478abd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615736} :answer-field/id #uuid "06ba1018-9742-5bb9-acaf-6e1c78a435f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "205a963f-bbd2-53a3-8b83-486e54732164" :question/math-academy-id "q-101962" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=5-4x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=5-4x.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=5-4(0)=5,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=5-4(1)=1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=5-4(2)=-3,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=5-4(3)=-7.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $1$ | $-3$ | $-7$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane: \n\n![](images/d8/d8b81418ee13fbf6ceda3bdb40b418db13fc751082bdcf861777a2935fd39209.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=5-4x.$\n\n![](images/d4/d42d80f53ee904ea12475ae64e9bde55845b7c9974a303535882f6f385478abd.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616135 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bcb3dd1-6148-5c1f-be1e-f39057f7270c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615667} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9f7940-5f45-51eb-bb68-3ca9ca95b853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615759} {:answer/id #uuid "8b0072cb-d327-5286-b618-8d59b8b3548b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615824} {:answer/id #uuid "e88f6523-92a5-56fb-b717-05fcd1e39403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615986} {:answer/id #uuid "f2db9b6d-6069-51b4-bb46-f5f46fab7e29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b0072cb-d327-5286-b618-8d59b8b3548b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615824} :answer-field/id #uuid "89d5fd1a-bf02-5b2a-ae04-b1e9df541f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "216263a8-c23a-531d-bde4-4319dde50257" :question/math-academy-id "q-109426" :question/problem "![](images/8c/8cfcac21fcb0fd0f40d5992d3632478b5eb9b459bc26c3769bc10ad0dedd7ddf.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(2,4),B(4,2)$ and $C(5,7).$ \n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(2,4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+2 \\\\ (4) & =(2)+2 \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(4,2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+2 \\\\ (2) & =(4)+2 \\\\ 2 & =6\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(5,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+2 \\\\ (7) & =(5)+2 \\\\ 7 & =7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "039ad3b7-e0db-5855-8a84-8b0927169c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "039ad3b7-e0db-5855-8a84-8b0927169c4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{9{e}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615578} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce8c475e-3d50-5c11-a7d2-89fd9be805ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616105}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "262ca3ad-35c3-5466-8b3c-a39ccd5205cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-348309" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9ed1cae3079318854aa49cd1fc41fc750d0abfb76f2c125d3801bae19b0d2bce.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve (shown above)\n\n$$\nx=3t{e}^{t},\\,y={t}^{2}+4t,\\,0\\le t<\\infty ,\n$$\n\nfind the derivative $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ at the point $P$ on the curve where $t=2.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,2}=\n$$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{t}(t+1),\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2t+4}{3{e}^{t}(t+1)}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $t=2$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx}{|}_{t\\,=\\,2} & =\\frac{2(2)+4}{3{e}^{2}(2+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+4}{3{e}^{2}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9{e}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14522f12-5450-5a3e-b078-c9a4081248ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/46/4629fc8e8101f98984ef7978f1f8a0ee01f7ed24711783f2118d966d5b94957e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615601} {:answer/id #uuid "41539724-70fa-569b-8796-4338bc3ebdd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/87/87312f0b0896006aeeec252b2cd227d40511e01e3f4fe41a38110900096c13a7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615672} {:answer/id #uuid "539144d0-3b2a-55ad-9586-8c3fb0cff874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/909b704166ab6bcd78ed60fd758c09b203060a36c63a27b91f70a70884413403.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615707} {:answer/id #uuid "dcafbcae-9ff0-57b5-b8ee-1af577cfebf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c7/c7a489eb4dadc7b43ee0cc30884a8c96701a233b1f0c8d186a41da316d416dbe.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615961} {:answer/id #uuid "f25cf8c5-12c1-5a6b-bdd0-da80dcb900f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c5/c5c357f0ff2aae1c43e29608e5edf5e0d163b8b966d624ce32ca237a144a43be.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "539144d0-3b2a-55ad-9586-8c3fb0cff874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/909b704166ab6bcd78ed60fd758c09b203060a36c63a27b91f70a70884413403.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615707} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c66aac6-cad0-56a9-897a-be6cd7f049c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5906158b-ea03-50d0-807a-3ed479ac1c09" :question/math-academy-id "q-54427" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=x-3.$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-3.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-3=-1$;\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-3=0$;\n\n- if $x=4$ then $y=(4)-3=1$;\n\n- if $x=5$ then $y=(5)-3=2.$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane would look like this: \n\n![](images/1f/1fe5f6ab820a248c9b2dbcee4e09a9ad80fa46baaf80d4d2ebe7f9978f67825e.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line $y=x-3.$\n\n![](images/90/909b704166ab6bcd78ed60fd758c09b203060a36c63a27b91f70a70884413403.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616175 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c94485d-87ed-561b-abd4-7e4df344fada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615692} {:answer/id #uuid "7541cf76-309c-5bbb-8c5e-0ae42dd0969e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615785} {:answer/id #uuid "845c6477-70de-5e18-8c97-19790c533e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615808} {:answer/id #uuid "9ed3287c-469b-5a95-922a-6948d0ba614c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615865} {:answer/id #uuid "e725ecf9-75c7-5889-bbbe-f2511a797fae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615980}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "845c6477-70de-5e18-8c97-19790c533e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615808} :answer-field/id #uuid "37af25cc-488d-540e-bf4a-7c9b91e21415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8fc44029-401d-5f68-9076-3e7174693561" :question/math-academy-id "q-102089" :question/problem "![](images/42/420e97ad7d5e83c368138eee90d180b40a9ec946c4336d561c428e25dcb8205d.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nI. $y=\\frac{3}{4}x+1$\n\nII. $y=4-\\frac{4}{3}x$\n\nIII. $y=\\frac{4}{3}x$" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, we can choose $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,4)$ and $(3,0)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/ff/ffd1eea07781890c1dd539e2e36f796d9b18bb4b05b33a903279b88b329f9082.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=\\frac{3}{4}x+1.$ \nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =\\frac{3}{4}(0)+1 \\\\ 4 & =1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{3}{4}x+1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=4-\\frac{4}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,4)$ and $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4) & =4-\\frac{4}{3}(0) \\\\ 4 & =4\\,✓ \\\\ (0) & =4-\\frac{4}{3}(3) \\\\ 0 & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=4-\\frac{4}{3}x$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $y=\\frac{4}{3}x.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $B(3,0)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0) & =\\frac{4}{3}(3) \\\\ 0 & =4\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\frac{4}{3}x$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equation that represented the line in the graph was $y=4-\\frac{4}{3}x,$ corresponding to answer choice II. Therefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616186 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "414c9477-6391-5f4c-8a53-14653150b7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0b/0bb2f7743ffde57c780cea44397184a0bc6406b1f8f7907fdff87b7568f1fe4c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615671} {:answer/id #uuid "8469dfdd-3516-5d6a-babf-d3618d3bcbd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7b/7bfca449f158ed9717bab694a2bbd72287b640e67f7b93783cc9ba4ac55c100d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615809} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbee385-67f1-55bc-8ad0-73d3c971fefc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0cfc4bba4867b40c4c38b0886c37bb5c4cd64d293530ece7c67cdb6349134013.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615863} {:answer/id #uuid "cceaca9b-1f01-5534-8657-5178b87c65f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f9e1f19f89e0f2ef4fc4360536e48ece24bb85b86e6000d66a7b89a088fc9ae.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615940} {:answer/id #uuid "f0931b99-db87-56d5-975c-c6e73949c939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/038b7ae0818e4c94f0792daa4579d241f05fb65c7fe5909d78731adfda4af55f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616000}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8469dfdd-3516-5d6a-babf-d3618d3bcbd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7b/7bfca449f158ed9717bab694a2bbd72287b640e67f7b93783cc9ba4ac55c100d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615809} :answer-field/id #uuid "2174fee2-7f0a-563d-8245-c06e4c96cd18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a743d9b3-eafb-57c5-bd1c-83170e03b4b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-54289" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-3?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(0)-3 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,-3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=6.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(6)-3 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(6,0).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-3.$\n\n![](images/5c/5c09dcad81445121f3ded344b6346f9375588166f8a80204cb77043da43ca6d0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "028bd90a-76b6-5db9-abcb-e69627471fbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/37/37733432d63aeb7b317f7ee6e926a26d50a9a7549b7a9472d15d838036efbc08.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615577} {:answer/id #uuid "2348992e-09a6-55a8-990c-a957891e4f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/24/24002951cdf941e86e2ed33ffb9d8e1b846abf613deb13364d48c65d3dc57de2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615625} {:answer/id #uuid "54b0283f-26d1-502e-94c8-0f1815c7873f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/70/701ca98fc439573f5fccc5edc20932a8ec48c0e15cacef020ecbfe5e5dafa6a5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615709} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f484e0-8933-5daf-84a6-259e58625c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc0678b52283b56dc53b4fc048e8ee955df3a514468f08a876ac279372feae3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615976} {:answer/id #uuid "ec0825c9-3f81-5ac1-a362-9236cf7202eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/33960e05da46abdaec9b3cb85f7511a05a216709bcc4e1f8ada4209b3a7a2c52.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615992}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4f484e0-8933-5daf-84a6-259e58625c2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc0678b52283b56dc53b4fc048e8ee955df3a514468f08a876ac279372feae3c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615976} :answer-field/id #uuid "e76aa168-8250-57f1-b5c5-aebe550e5543" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b0776edb-1d47-5f2e-a2e8-d56ffea6c187" :question/math-academy-id "q-54291" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=-2x+3?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+3 \\\\  & =-2(0)+3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is$(0,3).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be  $x=2.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-2x+3 \\\\  & =-2(2)+3 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(2,-1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-2x+3.$\n\n![](images/7f/7fe451811427028f9475bbcdfc24915848e0e627f19102604e253b44904c1b07.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616195 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0acc2c2a-2e3e-5e06-92e4-03671a95928e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/29/29c7f557bad970ce2452a2a1ccf86d047bc62b2497f0537c7501bb4f7cd47acb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615589} {:answer/id #uuid "2a708a0f-91ba-5c99-80ca-a342bca13f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/497d1c67fb3a322ae402f6dfa69c8b069d91177ddef6a5847e6dbee4cb93f995.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615636} {:answer/id #uuid "4304a192-0f74-5d2f-819c-fa395a51b2e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/49ee7ae87aa5ab5df3795a64b10daf209612f66291be93f6ec76fd80e23b4f31.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615676} {:answer/id #uuid "84430687-f2c7-5499-8f9f-284acb6dea7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c8/c879a6e75c73e619b5652ce736009c17e0520aec16ee955edc704857cedafa10.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615807} {:answer/id #uuid "9b6d5c4b-be1e-5e09-a701-93d7ef2ec6ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/325632c86f32cac746aadab66b4891338e571363488a662e05628a8d4872192f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a708a0f-91ba-5c99-80ca-a342bca13f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/49/497d1c67fb3a322ae402f6dfa69c8b069d91177ddef6a5847e6dbee4cb93f995.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615636} :answer-field/id #uuid "8db05102-5af3-5d8b-9cf6-12e0b307e7b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4872b6d-dfe7-551f-ad7d-aa105f7bca24" :question/math-academy-id "q-71674" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=1-2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=1-2x.$\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=1-2(0)=1$;\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=1-2(1)=-1$;\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=1-2(2)=-3$;\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=1-2(3)=-5.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $-1$ | $-3$ | $-5$ |\n\nPlotting these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane would look like this: \n\n![](images/83/839a5bfb3fe69ea3c02f24b4ad428b1db9b0c58e7cd043b370a19b2ff332347a.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line $y=1-2x.$\n\n![](images/49/497d1c67fb3a322ae402f6dfa69c8b069d91177ddef6a5847e6dbee4cb93f995.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27c11f6c-9d54-5262-a2c8-d10ded5ebcfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615630} {:answer/id #uuid "50e3c5a5-fec8-5fc9-8908-62c5a206b233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615698} {:answer/id #uuid "a535ddf2-83e5-5332-b4da-8eebd434ee97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615878} {:answer/id #uuid "c533c369-6acf-5723-81d4-3faf8a71f5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615925} {:answer/id #uuid "d4592775-1a26-5121-a72d-13cbd06ef789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50e3c5a5-fec8-5fc9-8908-62c5a206b233" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615698} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f9341de-77ce-5380-b4ef-edf16824bdec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2b0e3f4-391d-53d6-87c0-5b33f45abbe3" :question/math-academy-id "q-44507" :question/problem "![](images/22/2223ef6e2f8d208453646c3698009cc30271ca5725409c859138bede98985e29.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-3x+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,7)$, $B(4,3)$ and $C(2,-5).$ \n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+1 \\\\ (7) & =-3(-2)+1 \\\\ 7 & =7\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(4,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+1 \\\\ (3) & =-3(4)+1 \\\\ 3 & =-11\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+1 \\\\ (-5) & =-3(2)+1 \\\\ -5 & =-5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ does not lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616204 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47be34c4-56c9-55d2-8f7c-ec791551425a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615688} {:answer/id #uuid "5548efe9-1549-523f-b196-b8ce25601cc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615711} {:answer/id #uuid "6069fc73-49f1-53f7-ad48-3fea934dc579" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615732} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b856ef-7b7f-5ed0-809f-3875cd7425d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615921} {:answer/id #uuid "cb3fa2ea-feda-512a-a547-e5856a849f6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47be34c4-56c9-55d2-8f7c-ec791551425a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615688} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c455a62-a208-502b-963e-c2dd814610a1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616062}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdd6dfc6-1793-52f9-8ef2-11d27941c618" :question/math-academy-id "q-102140" :question/problem "![](images/53/53cfc55c22f9fb48802ff09133edd1fb0f406c00619df97cbb3a1f9737376c24.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(1,3),B(3,6)$ and $C(5,3).$ \n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(1,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (3) & =(1)+3 \\\\ 3 & =4\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(3,6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (6) & =(3)+3 \\\\ 6 & =6\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(5,3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+3 \\\\ (3) & =(5)+3 \\\\ 3 & =8\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ lies on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616210 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33ae9d8d-cd42-57a3-b0ef-b0926dc152c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615653} {:answer/id #uuid "63cfcb5a-e6dc-53fc-a1f8-9c1c802bb0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615741} {:answer/id #uuid "6e4835a4-f635-5b8b-927f-9ea25429a1bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615769} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5b8811-c3ce-54a0-b73f-d5fbcd9ae886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615911} {:answer/id #uuid "bf87f747-8175-5877-b379-bc4173bed87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63cfcb5a-e6dc-53fc-a1f8-9c1c802bb0dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615741} :answer-field/id #uuid "07421851-dc97-5233-8a20-c4c7ccc05ed3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dd84f514-1f21-547a-b304-ad218f21f58b" :question/math-academy-id "q-44505" :question/problem "![](images/d5/d58e330c54284f7f3df8b96976741558d42728eae2b3944315a9f6fbb8415054.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-10x-23?$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,-3)$, $B(1,-3)$ and $C(3,-3).$\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,-3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-10x-23 \\\\ (-3) & =-10(-2)-23 \\\\ -3 & =-3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-10x-23 \\\\ (-3) & =-10(1)-23 \\\\ -3 & =-33\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,-3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-10x-23 \\\\ (-3) & =-10(3)-23 \\\\ -3 & =-53\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ do not lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616214 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27554ed9-cd58-5206-ba6c-d21674ca8dc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/90/90b281b0fc99042e5b8069871c695d932c1fc4c8490ac1c3d8e80b85a031de2f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615629} {:answer/id #uuid "58b8ea25-00b1-5912-a12f-7dd273e61ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e25d3e17e015f41616d21570f6181f24bce6e07d4d33a12debbc2890cb0d7bb6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615718} {:answer/id #uuid "addfa6ef-4695-5b12-a889-76fc98540b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2ac43fe1cdc4cf704a9cd7e4332b6fcc30ed70b26d72c40475fbc4ca096add68.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615891} {:answer/id #uuid "cdfa54fe-6d09-5211-87e9-d8603f52800f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/45/45f2d0b7587eb0c822bca86560144795281cb1e5cc336cbdf93771ac0a47e763.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186615941} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b2b03d-f452-5bb6-8a46-b9bdf8bb1b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/5663413740a7562f357bde157e7613b9aa6a18fdf46ba590f6227baa91bf7519.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616001}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0b2b03d-f452-5bb6-8a46-b9bdf8bb1b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/5663413740a7562f357bde157e7613b9aa6a18fdf46ba590f6227baa91bf7519.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616001} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a017c3-8a9d-5cfa-8d82-14f752415749" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616068}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ecda4665-585d-5404-9dcb-5d02fd4c21d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-71797" :question/problem "Which of the following graphs shows the line $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+2?$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\n- For the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{3}x+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(0)+2 \\\\  & =0+2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,2).$\n\n- For the second point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=6.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{3}x+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(6)+2 \\\\  & =2+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(6,4).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{3}x+2.$\n\n![](images/6a/6ac6477bf097c6691715a4e38ee6bb400ede800a887d627b84c6ac45a12c4d43.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c59ab1b-f4c8-5a75-87e4-20893cd4b044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24(-9-4x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c59ab1b-f4c8-5a75-87e4-20893cd4b044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24(-9-4x)^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616326} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b9c5d6-db2e-54e6-84b8-bf2a0320e4db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "57a6783a-fc39-5ef5-8a1c-628f352f4ad2" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(-9-4x)^{6}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{6},\\,g=-9-4x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6g^{5},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=6g^{5}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  &=-24(-9-4x)^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b7bf8b1-ff38-5f11-bbcc-50fa3c64315d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12(3 x - 2)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616322} {:answer/id #uuid "3b7d9b20-6c95-5ef1-9f2f-5d156d52e4b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21(3 x - 2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616324} {:answer/id #uuid "44ea5da8-041a-5e5b-99cd-1fb7c91c60e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28(3 x - 2)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616325} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b17d71-4b32-5a53-8943-d88edbe9e11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9(3 x - 2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616330} {:answer/id #uuid "d5a8f75a-30e8-5ac1-8c2d-9aeb2e7e764a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(3 x - 2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3b17d71-4b32-5a53-8943-d88edbe9e11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9(3 x - 2)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616330} :answer-field/id #uuid "298df8c1-b7b3-5697-9024-df99fb83258d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616323}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a831160d-bd79-52f7-b589-31b6792f7366" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ when $f(x)=(3 x - 2)^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{3},\\,g=3 x - 2\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=3g^{2},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=3g^{2}\\cdot (3) \\\\  &=9(3 x - 2)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be2eabd-65d0-5a45-9ee9-05278e4b32b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616468} {:answer/id #uuid "50f00403-9325-5cc5-ac61-fc7dc12d5769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616511} {:answer/id #uuid "571b5136-5af4-5004-bb6e-2e8e622edf9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{8}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616526} {:answer/id #uuid "5c2e15a4-83c5-5114-a35d-af55b0cd8b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616538} {:answer/id #uuid "e418d87a-b3b9-56cc-aee4-113df2db0a18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e418d87a-b3b9-56cc-aee4-113df2db0a18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616777} :answer-field/id #uuid "da2b5851-1600-5483-ba86-e361b284b1fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1efb36d9-27aa-57f3-a19c-d15de20d9d10" :question/math-academy-id "q-15795" :question/problem "Which of the following parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ generate a circle of radius $4$ centered at the origin?" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=4.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77396a1d-ad66-580f-8d33-cb03838687c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\cos\\theta-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616586}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77396a1d-ad66-580f-8d33-cb03838687c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\cos\\theta-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616586} :answer-field/id #uuid "53835003-cde2-57ff-a69c-fea5b010cc07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616860} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c06218c4-7281-5ef4-bed3-15766556cebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin\\theta+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c06218c4-7281-5ef4-bed3-15766556cebd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin\\theta+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616722} :answer-field/id #uuid "68d642df-932b-57ac-b257-e3d7835a7877" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c76f0dc-d63d-5658-acb8-beb3b5e4325d" :question/math-academy-id "q-321937" :question/problem "![](images/40/402ba8432eca5bd5e15839d84c3ea58baf5500afa653e903b2abdcabb3eea92e.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $6$ centered at $(-2,5)$, as shown above. Construct a set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$ that traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(4,5).$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle of radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +a,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +b,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r+a,b).$\n\nIn our case, we have a circle of radius $6$ centered at the point $(-2,5).$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +5,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12e68944-8b42-519c-b87c-1b8fbfca1665" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-1={y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616415} {:answer/id #uuid "297902bb-93e5-5d86-a76d-34f11fcd9687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616442} {:answer/id #uuid "5d9b1705-e56f-5dea-8820-08137d0df983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\pm (x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616542} {:answer/id #uuid "c57c3f98-6e31-5ca7-8d8c-55b745eb0ce8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}-(x-1)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616734} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a9991c-a691-5f7c-bc9f-9563065ba622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3a9991c-a691-5f7c-bc9f-9563065ba622" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616776} :answer-field/id #uuid "7baafcd4-4aad-5851-9f46-c65b5a319a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616879}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51c65e6a-651d-5420-a16a-caee443b9832" :question/math-academy-id "q-71200" :question/problem "Find the equation of the level curve that passes through the point $N(1,1)$ for the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the function at $N$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =\\frac{2(1)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the level curve that passes through $N(1,1)$ is the $1$-level curve.\n\nRecall that the level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=1.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ 2x & ={x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+1+{y}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level curve that passes through $N(1,1)$ is the circle $(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d405f4c-df48-5898-8402-865bb1511b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616404} {:answer/id #uuid "62a770b5-3684-5c55-b7db-1bba731ccbba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{3\\pi }{2},2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616547} {:answer/id #uuid "824c10c5-dc4a-5f4e-afa6-1e8b60ff16ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616607} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b03ae3-840f-5d6e-aec6-68f4e6615d93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616677} {:answer/id #uuid "e2855918-3e2c-51d4-aae2-9062083e1b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d405f4c-df48-5898-8402-865bb1511b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616404} :answer-field/id #uuid "008eba65-7b93-5ef5-827b-c354e584c974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616823}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6748794a-9217-5dcf-805f-e901bd7cd42a" :question/math-academy-id "q-106295" :question/problem "![](images/3d/3db3257b5c00e722ea71f9973dc47994c01068ec29e95c045835e803ab3720b2.png)\n\nThe quarter-circle above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$  centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=5.$ So, the parametric equations of the *full* circle are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-circle, we associate the parameter $\\theta$ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the circle and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/a8/a8fc93176ea43d63a918e58ac43d545f620c64c9ed3c2b85589856125718d9f3.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta$ to $[\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the required quarter-circle.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-circle are \n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186616978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73b17926-b51c-5671-9153-44627f5e7ff3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=22\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=22\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616578} {:answer/id #uuid "82488b6f-db72-52c3-a322-db132734e996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616606} {:answer/id #uuid "9a8bd446-29a2-596b-b392-4f966bfa75f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616653} {:answer/id #uuid "adbd523e-7c01-552f-bcc3-5e11d61e0ed0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=11\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616690} {:answer/id #uuid "f9788cae-e0f6-5fa6-a75f-8c179b57d253" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82488b6f-db72-52c3-a322-db132734e996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=11\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616606} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fed142e-1bc4-51d0-a99a-e260ef8ac336" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68b849e9-dfc5-5d79-828a-d0b358643747" :question/math-academy-id "q-15798" :question/problem "![](images/24/244e3cebb0eb0607773af1696c31961e646977ecf2a52308e9ecdc8ae81994a5.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $11$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(11,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$ centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=11.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=11\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23729e4b-a502-5abe-be5f-2650ef30ef75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616432} {:answer/id #uuid "6f748177-15a5-56be-935a-506d3d9656ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616572} {:answer/id #uuid "718219fb-e2e2-5656-99ec-81d7d26dadae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616576} {:answer/id #uuid "9d38b368-4e96-5353-a485-3326bdcf14f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616657} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a79db5-3a00-5946-87a4-8c77024947f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d38b368-4e96-5353-a485-3326bdcf14f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616657} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f73a3f3-3a7c-5657-bdad-a013a24e5bba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186616890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d2005e3c-2f15-599f-b896-1f8653c918a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-6892" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the circle\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the circle, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy squaring the $x$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {x}^{2} & =(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =36{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy squaring the $y$-equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {y}^{2} & =(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2} \\\\  & =36{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =36{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +36{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =36({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ) \\\\  & =36(1) \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore the Cartesian equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ebf8caf-6f88-58e6-b6a7-9c8e361149bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617932} {:answer/id #uuid "5953ae37-a47b-5213-a42a-832f7da45479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617940} {:answer/id #uuid "65c02266-5027-53f0-815c-708cde0fbbef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617942} {:answer/id #uuid "bfcd8082-f5f2-5338-a0e4-a633099ebdd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617954} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4bf31e-0900-5c82-98a3-b6e289879746" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5953ae37-a47b-5213-a42a-832f7da45479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617940} :answer-field/id #uuid "163e87f4-3d02-568e-8528-407bf206291e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617931}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1fd43e88-79c8-59c9-ac52-5430abc60433" :question/problem "![](images/91/91f73d4130edb919d753352e6fb1d1a013709e28d62cdf30a0c8fc5b8fdf7e4c.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x-2$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(1,2)$, $B(-2,-6)$, $C(-4,-8)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(1,2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-2 \\\\ (2) &= 2(1)-2 \\\\ 2 &= 0 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-2 \\\\ (-6) &= 2(-2)-2 \\\\ -6 &= -6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-4,-8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-2 \\\\ (-8) &= 2(-4)-2 \\\\ -8 &= -10 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ lies on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617934 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bcadd79-1d59-504e-b82e-60891fbc927b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617937} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ffc9b3-b8d3-587e-a443-e1fc7b692026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617951} {:answer/id #uuid "be960ff4-5c55-52e4-ab06-378b59d656bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617953} {:answer/id #uuid "c3e2aefc-c2ac-518f-a4e2-9d040c9b69c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617957} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a1ca8d-d478-5a72-ab25-16d2864d8e60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617963}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bcadd79-1d59-504e-b82e-60891fbc927b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617937} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2c983b0-e619-5fb5-9f52-b7d09cd53c1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "396e0e91-d27c-5dba-8918-9d968b80f0d2" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b88f738026aa7528e4e25c5c36ebd48c7c9f6dd497478ae746555ea790bcf5f.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x-3$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(3,3)$, $B(0,-5)$, $C(-1,-5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(3,3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-3 \\\\ (3) &= 2(3)-3 \\\\ 3 &= 3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,-5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-3 \\\\ (-5) &= 2(0)-3 \\\\ -5 &= -3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-1,-5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x-3 \\\\ (-5) &= 2(-1)-3 \\\\ -5 &= -5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617943 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43978fd4-6c43-5a75-a5b4-9af83bd3360c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617936} {:answer/id #uuid "567f69ad-3ab7-5b9b-b0e2-b185c50ebaa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617939} {:answer/id #uuid "9558fd96-e6b5-501e-b521-70de60330dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617946} {:answer/id #uuid "a9f8d4a7-c23d-5990-a6bb-10e9b05c4f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617949} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e5082b-1a2b-5a30-9f78-5a9d210b65f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9558fd96-e6b5-501e-b521-70de60330dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617946} :answer-field/id #uuid "c154a9c1-f7d0-5bf5-bc54-cf4bdbcbb98d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617955}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7934e8c1-3564-5743-8080-fd2bcba84a83" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1bb11ff96613977acc678334ea9ffc163acc79fb771e36ab179392ca964aac59.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,-3)$, $B(4,1)$, $C(2,2)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,-3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ (-3) &= (-3) \\\\ -3 &= -3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(4,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ (1) &= (4) \\\\ 1 &= 4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x \\\\ (2) &= (2) \\\\ 2 &= 2 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617948 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125f968f-d28f-5f20-9777-724e0ec59289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617930} {:answer/id #uuid "4c64cec2-045f-5eb1-b315-c80ed5b2e927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617938} {:answer/id #uuid "8fae9338-6e48-55fb-952a-dc88cca704af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617945} {:answer/id #uuid "9626b0b9-43f2-5580-ad15-8204a8b8fee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617947} {:answer/id #uuid "ad60ce8d-66d0-5d13-a625-02ee535d9b4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9626b0b9-43f2-5580-ad15-8204a8b8fee2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617947} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c8bb1e6-0b52-54c5-bb4c-1ab7c0380e01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9edd7280-e29c-5912-8a35-4cb819fe08a1" :question/problem "![](images/15/1527d66e141103edd1a772b7cb6431f795ca58b02ad2ff3ba73b9f7cf6f9f63e.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=2x+5$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-4,-4)$, $B(0,5)$, $C(2,9)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-4,-4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x+5 \\\\ (-4) &= 2(-4)+5 \\\\ -4 &= -3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x+5 \\\\ (5) &= 2(0)+5 \\\\ 5 &= 5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,9)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= 2x+5 \\\\ (9) &= 2(2)+5 \\\\ 9 &= 9 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186617964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "617f4fb5-d247-58aa-8249-245f52072e72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617941} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa0c75b-35b8-559f-bc48-41ab09df0ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617944} {:answer/id #uuid "bd28c7c2-388e-56ea-90b9-5a7b2f4c63d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617952} {:answer/id #uuid "c164ca1b-9460-5416-9216-b2c1f821f43f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617956} {:answer/id #uuid "d4dd1149-5897-53c4-9c53-fbaf41c4f172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fa0c75b-35b8-559f-bc48-41ab09df0ba8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617944} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbbc9730-d785-5e13-853d-20a42d9da5c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186617958}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ffea0c1d-d629-5e9a-b451-0c1281465a42" :question/problem "![](images/b9/b9af9b389b7306f786a714929e92697313d5d335c701a136611992c34a456798.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=x-4$." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,-4)$, $B(3,-1)$, $C(2,-3)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,-4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x-4 \\\\ (-4) &= (0)-4 \\\\ -4 &= -4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(3,-1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x-4 \\\\ (-1) &= (3)-4 \\\\ -1 &= -1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(2,-3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= x-4 \\\\ (-3) &= (2)-4 \\\\ -3 &= -2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $B$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2761106d-36b4-5c43-b5ab-1a2ce627f560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/21/219c812445b41a8c04c9da56196886d054d27f6a67d8d892a969565e606003b8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618021} {:answer/id #uuid "50fcf253-83b0-58c3-a87e-ed8ee239f267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/933874b5bc27630d371a6f64957c6ba0160b0d4e4980ac9c40cee790afe52fcf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618027} {:answer/id #uuid "6453f893-c193-5be2-bf36-eb7a1d6fb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/aed04c3845df13431f4d64cd9587070ae4c2bc15e1802d00ca8fdc170f7987b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618030} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf671c3-82a6-5a8e-a46b-5d09cabe540b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4a/4abf642f37aefc73263e184ce0574a7da6929802c812f7f68f4ae8a1086bfe33.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618032} {:answer/id #uuid "90f02a68-9393-5aaf-9708-644171767f82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0a/0aaeb2c253855479ba93a06e578b65cdfbda04e64f1195e2d7690c214064494b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6453f893-c193-5be2-bf36-eb7a1d6fb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ae/aed04c3845df13431f4d64cd9587070ae4c2bc15e1802d00ca8fdc170f7987b2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618030} :answer-field/id #uuid "8773b33f-7eb4-588c-bbf8-558ae9d6c774" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618033}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "055d3748-f346-5d87-ad14-41330ebf61ae" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x+1.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x+1.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=2(0)+1=1,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)+1=3,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)+1=5,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)+1=7.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ | $7$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/35/35483254ead1f56d168138c1cf010a4f95112490b85113c01e6efcd3e5f3ee3e.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=2x+1.$\n\n![](images/ae/aed04c3845df13431f4d64cd9587070ae4c2bc15e1802d00ca8fdc170f7987b2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618023 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aaa3936-e4e5-562f-b45d-1dae2df516b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/136008a24d5aa868a9eb29c2d610aae5e169558b782913d7772027d73cffcb5c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618016} {:answer/id #uuid "20ef0741-7bcb-5f13-9c79-239bf70507ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/86/86a3e537726dd4896ed754aeb520e1017f98c858f3297bf77f3c2e4baa2a00ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618020} {:answer/id #uuid "91fd6e69-d757-5381-8152-d36ec39fe82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30af7776308a0bf8a76cbbfcededfe11b145f29c1edc0855c2f3c5339b201934.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618035} {:answer/id #uuid "a9aca89a-65a7-53f3-8a03-cf3d602c818e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/74/74a4fb1bed0ce21a6598a3e3dfb17575f5628db27c41be603c578d944a2711cb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618037} {:answer/id #uuid "d90adfec-283f-5edb-883d-ae8dad4f7f2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/3392ac8ff49b7eb76df268e88b6fc2f16a93ef4fada6bf85d703dea0ecec03dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91fd6e69-d757-5381-8152-d36ec39fe82e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/30/30af7776308a0bf8a76cbbfcededfe11b145f29c1edc0855c2f3c5339b201934.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618035} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6f4aea0-40a0-5226-b47e-2a61f3eaea60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38aaa941-d7f1-55ed-8304-6e91a8bf348a" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=-x.$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=-x.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=-(2)=-2,$\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=-(3)=-3,$\n\n- if $x=4$ then $y=-(4)=-4,$ and\n\n- if $x=5$ then $y=-(5)=-5.$\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-2$ | $-3$ | $-4$ | $-5$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/d2/d288b6b97a573fd2a526dad6241a85347a6e2071212340131d11e9d0f5e012f5.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=-x.$\n\n![](images/30/30af7776308a0bf8a76cbbfcededfe11b145f29c1edc0855c2f3c5339b201934.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186618040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12a13afb-615d-5da7-95ae-b40d6989fe17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26d63be2a0b276a05a9248caedfa06311cb473454c43559d6d51825e9f27d11b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618019} {:answer/id #uuid "3e9dd8c5-c2ef-57b0-9b5d-5280833cd64a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/b3/b399ef8d57fe10230b607aadbe7aeddb887ef9dd751d5211d19e4ad04b643e59.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618024} {:answer/id #uuid "4dfda7ff-5f21-52b0-a25b-c669bb7e09c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a5/a51fd419eee24f208f8500dbacceb6a07fce0be478defc519b5710ba357f8761.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618025} {:answer/id #uuid "599bed9e-feb0-55fe-a57a-4cc497f51d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c3/c347acd02793211c3feaf9b7374bbd28f94ebc917ed849e71582ecfe7f7e840d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618028} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a3fb52-bb3b-5e22-bab0-9f676c2ed8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d4/d44dc5fdcb4e1da94210c90ac0bbae4c888f7e377a5f7a94ab63c62067d3d802.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12a13afb-615d-5da7-95ae-b40d6989fe17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26d63be2a0b276a05a9248caedfa06311cb473454c43559d6d51825e9f27d11b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618019} :answer-field/id #uuid "0575a3c2-2b1f-55d7-adfa-3c9a7ff0d7a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186618014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c23acb85-09f4-598a-9c73-efb0eb948fdb" :question/problem "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=2x+2.$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=2x+2.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=2(1)+2=4,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=2(2)+2=6,$\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=2(3)+2=8,$ and\n\n- if $x=4$ then $y=2(4)+2=10.$\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ | $10$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/10/107054b3b3a3a52642416caa394926fb9e4ea8d4ca6906b45899a56fd771672b.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=2x+2.$\n\n![](images/26/26d63be2a0b276a05a9248caedfa06311cb473454c43559d6d51825e9f27d11b.png)"}]}
